Sure! To update a `break` node’s label to `"loopEnd"` (but only if it isn’t already `"loopEnd"`), you can use the `updateBreak` helper.  
Just supply the node you want to modify (as a JSON‑style string) and the new label. Here’s a quick example:

```javascript
// Suppose this is your break node in the AST (stringified)
const breakNode = '{"type":"BreakStatement","label":"oldLabel"}';

// Call the helper to update it
const updatedNode = updateBreak({
  node: breakNode,
  label: "loopEnd"
});

console.log(updatedNode);
```

If the node already has the label `"loopEnd"`, the helper will simply return the original node unchanged.

**What you need to do:**

1. Replace `breakNode` with the actual string representation of your break node.  
2. Run the snippet (or call the function directly in your environment).  

